 ## 8. Config ownership
 
-**The M3 gate: every control has exactly one declared owner.** A control the agent can read that also varies by arm is not an experiment; a control the agent sets that changes the mechanics of its own authority is not an ablation.
-
-| owner | controls |
-|---|---|
-| **Experiment** (run config, never agent-facing) | `b` per lever · lever on/off · `T_base`, `T_commandable`, `T_bounds` per lever · **`aggregate_fn`** · contextual & synergy channel on/off · size-control mode & sum-constraint method · divergence metric · sidecar richness · `complexityRatio` · `COMPXY_TEMP` · `nToKeep` / `capCoef` · `LLMOSES_RNG_SEED` · truncation policy (§9.2) |
-| **Agent** | utility values (per member, per atom, per row) · contextual entries when the channel is on · synergy entries when the channel is on · `T_requested` where commandable |
-| **Retired** | `λ` · `ε` · `W` · `direction` / `magnitude` |
-
-**`aggregate_fn` moves to experiment config.** It is the composition policy mapping atom utilities to combination weights — it determines what `b` *means*. An agent choosing its own aggregation semantics is choosing the units of its own authority, and arms whose mechanics vary per response are not comparable.
-
-### 8.1 Ingest validation — the silent-failure class
-
-Three findings shared one pattern: an optional schema field silently deciding whether a capability exists. Fix as a class.
-
-| case | required behaviour |
-|---|---|
-| contextual data present, `lever_weights` absent | **reject at ingest with an explicit error** — do not prune to `inert` |
